# A Final Attack after the Marksman's own shots, and the reason a Final Attack
# can have its own reach: GMS gives the split its own mobCount and hitbox, so
# even after Snipe, which hits one, it hits ten. Other Final Attacks land on the
# one enemy their swing picked, which final_attack_max_enemies reads as 1.
#
# The swings it follows are set by group, not a list of names. GMS names
# Piercing Arrow, Snipe and the cartridge, and those three carry the tag. High
# Speed Shot, Perfect Shot and Surge Bolt are left out on purpose.
#
# GMS's text says "Landing a hit with Full Burst Shot after using ..." and then
# lists the cartridge among the skills it follows, naming the skill as an
# alternative to itself. Grandis Library states it plainly (hits from those
# skills release the burst), and Final Aim's text ("triggered up to 13 times")
# only makes sense if the default is once per cast. So it is once per cast.
name: "Split Shot"
description:
  "Magically enchants your arrows to explode as they approach the enemy, "
  "releasing countless more arrows."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_MARKSMAN_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
final_attack_label: "Split Arrows"
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
follows_skill_tag: SKILL_TAG_MARKSMANSHIP
final_attack_max_enemies: 10
buff {
  duration_seconds: 72.0
  base {
    final_attack_chance: 1.0
    final_attack_pct: 6.06
    final_attack_lines: 5
    ied_pct: 0.25
  }
  per_level { final_attack_pct: 0.24 }
}
